Chemical and Biological Reaction Engineering — MIT 10.37 (@ic-mit-reaction: 0, is #reference, #part-of @ic-sources) { r_67AEXD9K1DJ46SV942PAZHZ4BZ
K. Dane Wittrup and William H. Green, Jr. Chemical and Biological Reaction Engineering, MIT 10.37, Spring 2007. [Complete public course](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-engineering-spring-2007/) · [Lecture notes](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-engineering-spring-2007/pages/lecture-notes/) · [Assignments](https://ocw.mit.edu/courses/10-37-chemical-and-biological-reaction-engineering-spring-2007/pages/assignments/).

Complete the published undergraduate programme and independently solve its problems/examinations. It joins stoichiometry, mechanisms, kinetics, reactor models, biological systems, catalysis and transport. The notes complement the whole Rawlings/Ekerdt text; campus readings or absent materials are not silently supplied by OCW.

Course level, teachers, scope and public resources were checked on 29 October 2026. MIT OCW's CC BY-NC-SA terms apply subject to component exceptions and separate external-book rights. Record the actual resource version. Nothing is mirrored and no full-course playback or future reader work is claimed.

